BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:launch-0d6ad64c-3aed-4041-b095-e1d951bc6d29@readout
DTSTAMP:20270128T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270129
SUMMARY:Launch: Aspera
DESCRIPTION:Electron · Rocket Lab Aspera houses an ultraviolet telescope 
 and will examine hot gas in the intergalactic medium\, thought to be cont
 ributing to the birth of stars and planets. Aspera will be the first NASA
  astrophysics mission to gather and map these ultraviolet light signature
 s\, potentially unlocking a deeper understanding of the origins of stars\
 , planets\, and life in the universe. Source: Launch Library 2 (The Space
  Devs).
LOCATION:Rocket Lab Launch Complex 1\, Mahia Peninsula\, New Zealand
URL:https://ll.thespacedevs.com/2.3.0/launches/0d6ad64c-3aed-4041-b095-e1d
 951bc6d29/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
